test hands-paint
# Hands: the colour tool. Chosen from the actions wheel ("Select Color Tool"), it paints the block the right hand points at
# with the right trigger and takes up that block's colour with the left trigger.
# World: Earth Planet (survival, on foot, in gravity). A large armor block is built ahead as the thing to paint. The angle of
# the "Select Color Tool" entry below is for Earth Planet's 19 entries (it is the fifth, 4 x 18.9 = 75.8 degrees clockwise
# from up): the "Actions wheel: opened" line lists the entries in order.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: a block to paint, and a build colour that is not the block's own ----------------------------------------

admin creativeTools
# out of the starter base, where nothing is built within 10 m, to build there
goto open
# the block is built in the selected colour, which the game keeps from world to world: first one unlike the paint
color 0.1 0.5 0.5
build LargeBlockArmorBlock 2.2 as Test block
goto Test block 2.2
color 0.6 0.3 0.2
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.25 1.2 -0.3
hand right 0.2 1.3 -0.3 -17 -4 0
wait 1
# Before: the block's colour, remembered.
read nearby LargeBlockArmorBlock 5
mark

# ---- The actions wheel: Select Color Tool ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

press left grip
wait 1
press left stick
wait 0.2
release left stick
wait 1
stick left 0.969 0.245
wait 0.7
release left grip
wait 0.3
stick left 0 0
wait 1.5
expect log Actions wheel: picked Select Color Tool within 5
expect log Colour tool on within 5

# ---- The right trigger paints the block pointed at --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

press right trigger
wait 0.5
release right trigger
wait 1.5
expect log Paint: within 5
read nearby LargeBlockArmorBlock 5
expect 0.colorMask moved > 0.01

# ---- The left trigger takes up the colour of the block pointed at -------------------------------------------------------------------------

press left trigger
wait 0.5
release left trigger
wait 1
expect log Paint: took the colour of the block pointed at within 5
expect no log Exception

test hands-tool-grinder
# Hands: the angle grinder in the right hand. The right trigger grinds what the hand points at: the character is shooting
# while it is pulled, and a small armor block ground long enough is gone.
# World: Earth Planet (survival, on foot, in gravity). A small armor block is built in the open at the hand's height, and the astronaut stands 1.1 m before it,
# the grinder in both hands.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: the grinder in toolbar slot 1, and one small armor block in front of the character -----------

admin creativeTools
give PhysicalGunObject/AngleGrinderItem
toolbar 1 PhysicalGunObject/AngleGrinderItem
# out of the starter base, where nothing is built within 10 m, to build there
goto open
# 1 m up, at the hand's height (a static block holds there; the game builds none into the ground)
build SmallBlockArmorBlock 2 1 as Test block
# 1.1 m before the block, facing it: its near side 85 cm ahead, clear of the grinder's muzzle, where the game's ray starts
goto Test block 1.1
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.25 1.2 -0.3
hand right 0.25 1.2 -0.3
wait 1

# ---- Take the grinder out with the tools wheel (slot 1) ----------------------------------------------------------------

press left grip
wait 1
stick left 0 1
wait 0.5
release left grip
wait 0.3
stick left 0 0
wait 2
read character
expect weapon.item contains AngleGrinderItem
expect log Hand tools: the AngleGrinder is held in the right hand within 5
# Before: the grinder is out, but not running.
expect weapon.shooting == false

# ---- The block is there, and the hand is not yet pointing at it -----------------------------------------------------------

read nearby SmallBlockArmorBlock 3
expect 0.subtype == SmallBlockArmorBlock

# ---- The right hand points straight ahead at the block (its near side 85 cm ahead, at the hand's height) ------------------------
# the left hand out of reach of the grip first, so the line below comes with the right hand where it will grind from
hand left -0.6 0.8 0.3
wait 0.5
hand right 0 1.2 -0.2
wait 1.5
# ---- The left hand takes the grinder's second grip, as the game's LeftHand spot has it: one-handed, a grinder kicks off the block --
# The plugin says where the second grip is as the left hand comes within reach of it: the left hand comes up near it, then
# goes onto it.
hand left -0.15 1.15 -0.25
wait 1
remember grip log '/Two-hand: Left hand within .* of the AngleGrinder.s grip .* the grip at stage \((\S+), (\S+), (\S+)\) m/'
hand left {grip}
wait 0.5
press left grip
wait 0.5
expect log Two-hand: Left hand took the AngleGrinder by its grip within 5
# ---- The trigger -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
press right trigger
wait 1
read character
expect weapon.shooting == true
# Grinding takes a while: hold on.
wait 12
release right trigger
release left grip
wait 1
read character
expect weapon.shooting == false
read nearby SmallBlockArmorBlock 3
expect result == []
expect no log Exception

test hands-tools-wheel
# Hands: the tools wheel on foot. Holding the left grip in empty air puts the toolbar up as a wheel; the left stick picks a
# slot, and letting go of the grip or pulling a trigger takes that tool in the right hand. The middle is the empty hand.
# World: Earth Planet (survival, on foot, in gravity). Three tools go into the inventory and the first three toolbar slots.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: a welder, an angle grinder and a hand drill in the first three slots of the toolbar ----------

give PhysicalGunObject/WelderItem
give PhysicalGunObject/AngleGrinderItem
give PhysicalGunObject/HandDrillItem
toolbar 1 PhysicalGunObject/WelderItem
toolbar 2 PhysicalGunObject/AngleGrinderItem
toolbar 3 PhysicalGunObject/HandDrillItem
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

# Headset level; the left hand out in front of the left shoulder in empty air (nothing to grab there), the right at rest.
head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.25 1.2 -0.3
hand right 0.25 1.2 -0.3
wait 1
# Before: nothing in the hand.
read character
expect weapon == null

# ---- Slot 1 (straight up on the wheel): the left stick up, then let go of the grip -> the welder ----------------------

press left grip
wait 1
read screen
expect type == SlotWheelScreen
stick left 0 1
wait 0.5
release left grip
wait 0.3
stick left 0 0
wait 2
expect log Toolbar wheel: activated slot 1 (grip let go) within 5
read character
expect weapon.item contains WelderItem

# ---- Slot 2 (40 degrees clockwise of up): the grinder replaces the welder -------------------------------------------------

press left grip
wait 1
stick left 0.643 0.766
wait 0.5
release left grip
wait 0.3
stick left 0 0
wait 2
expect log Toolbar wheel: activated slot 2 (grip let go) within 5
read character
expect weapon.item contains AngleGrinderItem

# ---- Slot 3 (80 degrees): chosen with the stick and taken with the right trigger instead of the grip -----------------------

press left grip
wait 1
stick left 0.985 0.174
wait 0.5
press right trigger
wait 0.2
release right trigger
release left grip
stick left 0 0
wait 2
expect log Toolbar wheel: activated slot 3 (right trigger) within 5
read character
expect weapon.item contains HandDrillItem

# ---- B cancels: the wheel closes and the drill stays in the hand; the right stick sideways turns the page ------------------

press left grip
wait 1
stick right 1 0
wait 0.5
stick right 0 0
expect log Toolbar wheel: page 2 of within 5
stick right -1 0
wait 0.5
stick right 0 0
expect log Toolbar wheel: page 1 of within 5
press right b
wait 0.2
release right b
release left grip
wait 1.5
expect log Toolbar wheel: closing within 5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
read character
expect weapon.item contains HandDrillItem

# ---- The middle is the empty hand: push the stick out, bring it back to the middle, pull the trigger -> hands empty -------

press left grip
wait 1
stick left 0 1
wait 0.5
stick left 0 0
wait 1
press right trigger
wait 0.2
release right trigger
release left grip
wait 2
expect log Toolbar wheel: empty hand (right trigger) within 5
read character
expect weapon == null
expect no log Exception

test hands-tool-welder-drill
# Hands: the welder and the hand drill in the right hand. Each is taken out with the tools wheel, is held in the right hand
# by the astronaut's wrist, aims where the hand points, and works while the right trigger is pulled.
# World: Earth Planet (survival, on foot, in gravity). Nothing is built; the hand points at the ground ahead.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: a welder in toolbar slot 1 and a hand drill in slot 2 ------------------------------------------

give PhysicalGunObject/WelderItem
give PhysicalGunObject/HandDrillItem
toolbar 1 PhysicalGunObject/WelderItem
toolbar 2 PhysicalGunObject/HandDrillItem
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.25 1.2 -0.3
# The right hand low, pointing forward and down at the ground about 1.5 m ahead.
hand right 0.25 1.1 -0.3 0 -30 0
wait 1

# ---- The welder: slot 1 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

press left grip
wait 1
stick left 0 1
wait 0.5
release left grip
wait 0.3
stick left 0 0
wait 2
read character
expect weapon.item contains WelderItem
expect log Hand tools: the Welder is held in the right hand within 5
# Before: not welding.
expect weapon.shooting == false
press right trigger
wait 1.5
read character
expect weapon.shooting == true
# The shot goes where the hand points, not where the head looks.
expect log Hand tools: shot direction from the hand within 5
release right trigger
wait 1
read character
expect weapon.shooting == false

# ---- The hand drill: slot 2 ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

press left grip
wait 1
stick left 0.643 0.766
wait 0.5
release left grip
wait 0.3
stick left 0 0
wait 2
read character
expect weapon.item contains HandDrillItem
expect log Hand tools: the HandDrill is held in the right hand within 5
expect weapon.shooting == false
press right trigger
wait 1.5
read character
expect weapon.shooting == true
release right trigger
wait 1
read character
expect weapon.shooting == false
expect no log Exception

test perf-standing-still
# Frame rate: standing still in a busy base, the headset gets its frames. The plugin reports every ten seconds how many
# frames the headset asked for and how many were drawn ("Perf 10.0 s [Focused]: N frames asked, M submitted (P%); frame
# cycle A ms avg / B p95 ..."). The window read is the newest after half a minute, past the world's loading.
# This guards against a change that makes the frames slower; it does not stand for a real headset's rate, which is
# measured in one.
# World: Earth Planet (survival; the astronaut starts in the starter base, with its lights, screens and grids around).

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60
head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.25 1.0 -0.2
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.2
wait 35
remember submitted log '/Perf 10.0 s \[Focused\]: \d+ frames asked, \d+ submitted \((\d+)%\)/'
remember p95 log '/Perf 10.0 s \[Focused\]: .* frame cycle [\d.]+ ms avg / ([\d.]+) p95/'
# Nearly every frame the headset asked for was drawn, none of them very late.
expect number {submitted} >= 95
expect number {p95} <= 40
expect no log Exception

test screens-inventory-pull
# Screens: a tool or gun pulled out of the inventory into the hand. With the laser on one in your own inventory, the grip
# squeezed and the hand drawn back toward you (15 cm) puts it in the hand through the game's own switch to that item.
# World: Earth Planet (survival, on foot). A pistol is given so the inventory surely holds a gun; the hand starts empty.
# The plugin says where the item is on the panel once the inventory page is shown, as in screens-inventory-toolbar.vrtest.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: a gun in the inventory ----------------------------------------------------------------------

give PhysicalGunObject/SemiAutoPistolItem
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.25 1.0 -0.3
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 1
# Before: nothing in the hand.
read character
expect weapon == null
key I
wait 2
read screens
expect result contains MyGuiScreenTerminal

remember tool log '/Inventory toolbar: on the panel, .* the first tool or gun you carry, (\S+), at stage/' within 10
remember toolAt log '/Inventory toolbar: on the panel, .* the first tool or gun you carry, \S+, at stage \((\S+), (\S+), (\S+)\) m/' within 10

# ---- A grip let go before the pull takes nothing -------------------------------------------------------------------------

hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.2 toward {toolAt}
wait 1
expect log Laser: pointing at the panel within 5
press right grip
wait 0.5
expect log /Inventory pull: Right grip on the .* in the inventory/ within 5
release right grip
wait 0.5
expect log Inventory pull: let go of the within 5
read character
expect weapon == null

# ---- The grip, then the hand drawn back 25 cm: it comes into the hand -------------------------------------------------------

press right grip
wait 0.5
hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.1 toward {toolAt}
wait 0.3
hand right 0.1 1.55 0.05 toward {toolAt}
wait 1
expect log came out of the inventory into the Right hand within 5
# The grip was the pull's, never the right mouse button.
expect no log Laser: right button down
release right grip
wait 0.5
read character
expect weapon.item contains {tool} within 5
expect no log Exception

key Escape
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

test screens-inventory-toolbar
# Screens: the toolbar on the inventory screen. In VR the inventory shows the toolbar's slots along its bottom; a hand tool
# or gun dragged with the laser's trigger from your inventory onto slot 3 goes in slot 3, as the G menu puts it there.
# World: Earth Planet (survival, on foot). A pistol is given so the inventory surely holds a gun; slot 3 is emptied first.
# The plugin says, once the inventory page is shown, where the toolbar's slots and the first tool or gun you carry are
# on the panel; the right hand, before the face at 0.1 1.55 -0.2, points at each.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: a gun in the inventory and nothing in slot 3 -----------------------------------------------

give PhysicalGunObject/SemiAutoPistolItem
toolbar 3
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.25 1.0 -0.3
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 1
expect headset steady
headset no-inventory.png
key I
wait 2
read screens
expect result contains MyGuiScreenTerminal
expect log Inventory toolbar: shown on the inventory page within 5

# ---- Where the inventory is drawn: standing in the world ahead, at the menu distance, and staying there ----------------

# A menu opens 2 m ahead of the head (Menu distance), level, at the height of the eyes, 60 degrees wide (Menu width),
# and stays where it opened while the head turns (Rendering/WorldMenu.cs).
headset inventory.png
expect headset new depth 1.5 2.6
expect headset new at 0 0 12
expect headset new size 35 75
head 0 1.6 0 20 0
wait 1
headset inventory-head-turned.png
expect headset new follows world
head 0 1.6 0
wait 1
# Before: slot 3 is empty.
read toolbar
remember before items

# ---- Where the first tool or gun and slot 3 are ------------------------------------------------------------------------

remember tool log '/Inventory toolbar: on the panel, .* the first tool or gun you carry, (\S+), at stage/' within 10
remember toolAt log '/Inventory toolbar: on the panel, .* the first tool or gun you carry, \S+, at stage \((\S+), (\S+), (\S+)\) m/' within 10
remember slot log '/Inventory toolbar: on the panel, its slots at stage .* 3 \((\S+), (\S+), (\S+)\), 4 /' within 10

# ---- The trigger on the tool, the hand turned to slot 3, the trigger let go ------------------------------------------

hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.2 toward {toolAt}
wait 1
expect log Laser: pointing at the panel within 5
press right trigger
wait 0.3
# Turning past the hold that keeps a click from being a drag, then on to slot 3.
hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.2 toward {slot}
wait 0.5
hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.2 toward {slot}
wait 0.5
release right trigger
wait 1
expect log /Inventory toolbar: .* put in slot 3/ within 5
read toolbar
expect items != {before}
expect items contains {tool}
expect no log Exception

key Escape
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

test screens-main-menu-loading
# Screens: the main menu and loading, in VR. Leaving a world for the main menu keeps the VR session and shows the menu in
# the headset (no scene, the menu panel in front of both eyes); loading a world from there brings the astronaut back with
# the headset still on.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: nothing built. The game menu is opened with the keyboard by the harness (the simulated Index
# ---- has no Menu button; README, Controls); this file tests what the headset shows, not how the menu is opened.

log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
wait 3
# The world in the headset, for the main menu to differ from.
headset world.png
expect headset bright

# ---- Out to the main menu -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

key Escape
wait 1.5
click Exit to Main Menu
wait 1
# The game asks to be sure; "Yes" leaves.
click Yes
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenMainMenu within 60
wait 3

# The VR session is still up, and the headset shows the menu (not the world, not black).
expect session focused within 10
headset menu.png
expect headset bright
expect headset changed

# ---- And back into a world, loaded from the main menu with the headset on ------------------------------------------------

world game:Earth Planet
expect session focused within 60
wait 3
headset back.png
expect headset bright
read character
expect health >= 1
expect state == standing
expect no log Exception

test screens-mouse-and-laser
# Screens: the mouse and the laser share a menu's cursor (LINUX_TESTS.md, "Mouse in VR menus"). The mouse takes the cursor
# when it moves; the right hand's laser takes it when its trigger is pulled on the menu and keeps it; the mouse takes it
# back, going on from where the laser left it.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: nothing built. A menu is opened with the keyboard by the harness (the inventory, I), because
# ---- the file tests who holds its cursor, not how it is opened.

log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
# The right hand rests below the menu, aimed down.
hand left -0.25 1.0 -0.3
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 1
key I
wait 2
read screens
expect result contains MyGuiScreenTerminal
# The inventory stands in the world ahead of the eyes, level, at the menu distance.
expect log Menu opened; panel placed within 5
# The right hand at eye height before the face, aimed straight ahead: its laser meets the panel near its middle.
hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.2 0 0
wait 1
expect log Laser: pointing at the panel within 5

# ---- The mouse moves: it has the cursor -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Before: nothing has said the mouse holds the cursor.
expect no log Laser: the mouse moved
mouse 500 300
wait 1
expect log Laser: the mouse moved, so the mouse has the cursor within 5
read cursor
expect result contains MyGuiControl

# ---- The hand moves without pressing: the mouse keeps the cursor ----------------------------------------------------------

hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 0.5
hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.2 0 0
wait 1
expect no log Laser: a press on the panel

# ---- The trigger on the menu: the laser takes the cursor and clicks there --------------------------------------------------

press right trigger
wait 0.3
release right trigger
wait 1
expect log Laser: a press on the panel, so the laser has the cursor within 5
expect log Laser: left button down at within 5

# ---- The mouse moves again: it goes on from where the laser was, with no jump -------------------------------------------

mouse 520 310
wait 1
expect log Laser: the mouse goes on from the laser within 5
expect no log Exception

key Escape
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

test screens-options-vr
# Screens: Options > VR. The game's Options screen has a VR button, it opens the plugin's settings screen on its tabs,
# and leaving by OK keeps the settings and writes the settings file. Then Headset layers in the desktop window, turned off
# and back on: the window says it shows the eye alone.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: nothing built. The simulated Index has no Menu button apps can use (README, Controls), so the
# ---- game menu is opened with the keyboard by the harness; this file tests the Options screens, not the opening.

log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
expect headset steady
headset no-menu.png
key Escape
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenMainMenu

# The game menu stands in the world: 2 m ahead of the head (Menu distance), level, at the height of the eyes, and it
# stays where it opened while the head turns (Rendering/WorldMenu.cs).
headset game-menu.png
expect headset new depth 1.5 2.6
expect headset new at 0 0 15
head 0 1.6 0 20 0
wait 1
headset game-menu-head-turned.png
expect headset new follows world
head 0 1.6 0
wait 1

# ---- Options, then the plugin's VR button ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

click Options
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenOptionsSpace
click VR
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == VROptionsScreen
# The screen's tab control has five tabs: Display, Comfort, Controls, Hands, Interface (Gui/VROptionsTabs.cs).
read screen
expect result contains VROptionsTabs

# Leave on the last tab, as a player would look through them.
set VROptionsTabs 4
wait 1

# ---- OK keeps the settings and writes the file -------------------------------------------------------------------------

click OK
wait 1.5
expect log VR options: leaving, nothing changed within 5
expect log Settings saved to within 5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenOptionsSpace
expect no log VR options: no tab line
expect no log Exception

# Back out of Options and the game menu.
key Escape
wait 1
key Escape
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

# ---- Headset layers in the desktop window off: logged, and put back ----------------------------------------------------

include vr-option.inc mirrorLayers false isChecked was_mirrorLayers
expect log '/Desktop window: the headset.s layers are not drawn/' within 5
expect no log Exception

cleanup
include vr-option.inc mirrorLayers {was_mirrorLayers} isChecked _

test screens-wheels-open
# Screens: the tools wheel and the actions wheel. Holding the left grip in empty air opens the tools wheel, clicking the
# left stick while it is open turns it into the actions wheel, and B closes it.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: the astronaut on foot with nothing in hand. Nothing is built. --------------------------------

log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

# Looking down at the hands, so the wheels are in view: the left hand is then about 0.5 m ahead of the eyes, 27 degrees
# left of the middle of the view and 8 below it.
head 0 1.6 0 0 -45
hand left -0.25 1.2 -0.3
hand right 0.25 1.2 -0.3
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
expect headset steady
headset no-wheel.png

# ---- Tools wheel: hold the left grip in empty air --------------------------------------------------------------------

press left grip
wait 1
read screen
expect type == SlotWheelScreen
# The toolbar's wheel is in the left hand: near, to the left of the view.
headset tools-wheel.png
expect headset new depth 0.2 1.0
expect headset new at -27 -8 20

# ---- Actions wheel: click the left stick while the tools wheel is open ----------------------------------------------

press left stick
wait 0.2
release left stick
wait 1
read screen
expect type == ActionsWheelScreen
expect log Actions wheel: opened at the left hand within 5
# The actions wheel is where the hand was when it opened (Gui/ActionsWheel.cs: at the grip, facing the head), and stays
# there until it closes: the view moves past it as the head looks further down. What is new against the tools wheel is
# what the actions wheel shows in its place.
headset actions-wheel.png
expect headset new depth 0.2 1.0
expect headset new at -27 -8 20
head 0 1.6 0 0 -60
wait 1
headset actions-wheel-look-down.png
expect headset new follows world
head 0 1.6 0 0 -45
wait 1

# ---- B closes it, with nothing chosen: no tool changed and the game has the focus --------------------------------------

press right b
wait 0.2
release right b
release left grip
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
read character
expect weapon == null
expect no log Exception

test screens-wrist-panel
# Screens: the wrist panel. Y (the left controller's upper button) opens the quick actions on a panel over the left wrist
# and Y again closes it; the right hand's laser and trigger press its tiles: Dampeners switches the dampeners, Inventory,
# Terminal and the G menu open their screens, which stand in the world ahead of the eyes, and B goes back out of them.
# The panel follows the left hand: with the hand where this file holds it, the panel's middle is 0.3 m from the right
# hand placed and turned as below, square on, and 0.3 m wide (1920 GUI pixels); each tile's place on it is the plugin's
# grid of 3 by 4 tiles (QuickActionsScreen.Layout).

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: the astronaut on foot in gravity (Earth Planet starts so). Nothing is built. ---------------

# Dampeners on, so the Dampeners tile has something to switch off.
dampeners on
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

# ---- Y opens and closes the panel -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Headset level, the left hand held out low before the body, the right hand resting below, aimed down.
head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.2 1.1 -0.35
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 1
# Before: only the game is up.
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
# Index's left B is the Y button.
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == QuickActionsScreen
expect log Wrist panel: opened (Y), 12 tiles within 5
expect log Menu opened on the wrist within 5
# Y again closes it.
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
expect log Wrist panel: closed (Y) within 5

# ---- Where the panel is drawn: on the left wrist, near, low and to the left, and it stays with the hand ----------------

# Looking down at the left hand, as a player does to use the panel. With the hand where this file holds it, the panel's
# middle is about 0.5 m ahead of the eyes, 18 degrees left of the middle of the view and 10 below it, and it is 0.3 m
# wide, about 35 degrees (Rendering/WorldMenu.cs, WristPose).
head 0 1.6 0 0 -45
wait 1
expect headset steady
headset wrist-closed.png
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == QuickActionsScreen
headset wrist-open.png
expect headset new depth 0.25 0.8
expect headset new at -18 -10 15
expect headset new size 20 50
# Looking further down, the panel stays on the wrist: the view moves past it, as it does past the world.
head 0 1.6 0 0 -60
wait 1
headset wrist-look-down.png
expect headset new follows world
# Y closes it, and the head is level again for the rest of the test.
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
head 0 1.6 0
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

# ---- The laser presses a tile: Dampeners ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

read character
expect dampeners == true
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 0.5
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == QuickActionsScreen
# The right hand's laser on the Dampeners tile, and its trigger.
hand right -0.128 1.438 -0.013 -36.5 -56.1
wait 1
expect log '/Laser: pointing at the panel, GUI [(]3[0-9][0-9], 6[0-9][0-9][)]/' within 5
press right trigger
wait 0.2
release right trigger
wait 1.5
# The game's own Dampeners control was pressed and the panel closed.
expect log '/Wrist panel: .Dampeners. read by the game/' within 5
read character
expect dampeners == false
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

# ---- The tiles that open screens: Inventory, Terminal, G menu, each in the world ahead -------------------------------

hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 0.5
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == QuickActionsScreen
# The right hand's laser on the Inventory tile, and its trigger.
hand right -0.158 1.473 -0.054 -36.5 -56.1
wait 1
expect log '/Laser: pointing at the panel, GUI [(]3[0-9][0-9], 2[0-9][0-9][)]/' within 5
press right trigger
wait 0.2
release right trigger
wait 1.5
read screens
expect result contains MyGuiScreenTerminal
expect log Menu opened; panel placed within 5
# B goes back: the screen closes and the game has the focus again.
press right b
wait 0.2
release right b
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 0.5
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == QuickActionsScreen
# The right hand's laser on the Terminal tile, and its trigger.
hand right -0.082 1.473 -0.111 -36.5 -56.1
wait 1
expect log '/Laser: pointing at the panel, GUI [(]9[0-9][0-9], 2[0-9][0-9][)]/' within 5
press right trigger
wait 0.2
release right trigger
wait 1.5
read screens
expect result contains MyGuiScreenTerminal
press right b
wait 0.2
release right b
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

# G menu: some screen other than the game and the panel has the focus.
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 0.5
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == QuickActionsScreen
# The right hand's laser on the G menu tile, and its trigger.
hand right -0.006 1.473 -0.167 -36.5 -56.1
wait 1
expect log '/Laser: pointing at the panel, GUI [(]1[45][0-9][0-9], 2[0-9][0-9][)]/' within 5
press right trigger
wait 0.2
release right trigger
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type != MyGuiScreenGamePlay
expect type != QuickActionsScreen
press right b
wait 0.2
release right b
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
# The datapad is left out of this release: nothing of it ran.
expect no log Datapad
expect no log Exception

test seats-camera-block-view
# Looking through a camera block: the eyes go to a still screen showing the camera, a right-stick flick switches camera,
# the stick up zooms, and holding Y returns to the character. Drill Ship Atmosphere mk.1's two cameras from Earth Planet.
plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- Setup: the head up, the world on the screen ---------------------------------------------------------------
admin creativeTools
# Earth Planet's ships belong to the world's own identity: the game lets the player control them once they own them
own Drill Ship Atmosphere mk.1
# remote control and cameras reach a ship only through its antenna, which this one has off
switch Drill Ship Antenna on
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60
head 0 1.6 0
wait 2
headset world.png
expect headset bright

# ---- View through the bow camera (the terminal's View action, a setup step) -------------------------------------------
# the camera's View button in the terminal
control Camera Bow on Drill Ship Atmosphere mk.1
wait 2
expect log VR controls: camera over on foot within 5
expect log Forced view: on (the view is a camera block within 5
headset camera.png
expect headset changed

# ---- Flick the right stick right: the next camera, then left: the previous one ----------------------------------------
stick right 1 0
wait 0.3
stick right 0 0
wait 0.5
expect log Camera view: right stick flicked right, the next camera (SWITCH_RIGHT) within 5
stick right -1 0
wait 0.3
stick right 0 0
wait 0.5
expect log Camera view: right stick flicked left, the previous camera (SWITCH_LEFT) within 5

# ---- The stick up zooms in while held, down zooms out ----------------------------------------------------------------
stick right 0 1
wait 1
expect log Camera view: right stick: zoom in (CAMERA_ZOOM_IN) held within 5
stick right 0 0
wait 0.5
expect log Camera view: right stick: zoom let go within 5
stick right 0 -1
wait 1
expect log Camera view: right stick: zoom out (CAMERA_ZOOM_OUT) held within 5
stick right 0 0
wait 0.5

# ---- Hold Y: back to the character and the world ----------------------------------------------------------------------
press left b
wait 0.8
release left b
wait 2
expect log Forced view: over within 5
expect log VR controls: on foot within 5
headset back.png
expect headset changed
expect headset bright

test seats-cockpit-hand-flight
# Flying from a cockpit with the buttons: in a cockpit that has a cockpit rig (the small cockpit here), A raises the ship and
# the grips roll it, with the thumbsticks left to the rig's own sticks. Sat down by the game's Use (a setup step); the
# hand entry is tested in seats-pilot-seat-enter-leave. Drill Ship Atmosphere mk.1 from Earth Planet.
plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- Setup: the ship's cockpit, and sit in it -----------------
admin creativeTools
# Earth Planet's ships belong to the world's own identity: the game lets the player control them once they own them
own Drill Ship Atmosphere mk.1
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60
head 0 1.6 0
wait 1
# the game's Use on the cockpit (the ship stands high on its landing gear, out of reach from the ground)
control Cockpit on Drill Ship Atmosphere mk.1
wait 2
read character
expect state == sitting
expect controlledEntity.type == MyCockpit
expect log VR controls: ship controller (Cockpit) within 5
wait 1

# ---- A held raises the ship ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
read grid Drill Ship Atmosphere mk.1
mark
press right a
wait 3
release right a
read grid Drill Ship Atmosphere mk.1
expect position moved > 0.5

# ---- Right grip rolls the ship: the pilot's up turns (the seat turns with the ship) ----------------------------------
# Hands kept at the sides, away from the cockpit's sticks.
hand left -0.3 0.9 -0.1
hand right 0.3 0.9 -0.1
read character
mark
press right grip
wait 2
release right grip
wait 0.5
read character
expect up moved > 0.05

# ---- Hold Y to get up ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
press left b
wait 0.8
release left b
wait 2
read character
expect state != sitting

test seats-cockpit-head-clamp
# In a seat the head is held round the pilot's head: leaning far out of the seat does not take the eyes through the
# cockpit's glass or floor. The plugin says how far it held the head.
plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- Setup: a pilot's seat of our own, built before the character ---------------------------------------------
admin creativeTools
# out of the starter base, where nothing is built within 10 m, to build there
goto open
build LargeBlockCockpitSeat 3 as TestClampSeat
goto TestClampSeat 1.0
wait 2
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60
head 0 1.6 0
hand right 0 1.3 -0.6
wait 1

# ---- Sit down with the right grip (see seats-pilot-seat-enter-leave for the reach) ---------------------------
press right grip
wait 1.5
release right grip
wait 1
read character
expect state == sitting
# Sitting still, nothing is held.
expect no log Seat clamp: head held

# ---- Lean a metre and a half forward and to the side: far further than the seat lets the head go ---------------
head 0.6 1.6 -1.5
wait 2
expect log Seat clamp: head held within 5

# ---- Back in the seat, then get up -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
head 0 1.6 0
press left b
wait 0.8
release left b
wait 1.5
read character
expect state != sitting

test seats-cryo-pod
# Getting into a cryo chamber with the hands and out of it again with Y held.
# The cryo chamber is its own kind of seat (the game's cryo pod), so the controls label names it.
plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- Setup: the station's cryo chamber (a cryo chamber is used only with power, which one built on its own grid has none of) --
admin creativeTools
# Earth Planet's station belongs to the world's own identity: the game lets the player use it once they own it
own EarthEasyStation
# Stand before it, facing it. The pod's door is low and ahead, so the hand reaches down-forward.
goto Cryo Chamber 1.0
wait 2
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60
head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.25 1.2 -0.3
hand right 0 1.3 -0.6
wait 1

# ---- Before: on foot, not in any seat ------------------------------------------------------------------------
read character
expect state != sitting
expect controlledEntity == null

# ---- Reach the seat with the right hand and grip: the game's Use, so the character sits ------------------------
# (Hand coordinates are a first guess; the log line "Grab use: Right palm ... box middle at tracking x,y,z" says where
# the seat's use spot is, head-relative, to tune them.)
press right grip
wait 1.5
release right grip
wait 1

# ---- After: seated in the block, and the hands' controls are the ship's ------------------------------------------
read character
expect state == sitting
expect controlledEntity.type == MyCryoChamber
expect log VR controls: ship controller (CryoChamber) within 5

# ---- Leave: hold Y (left B) for half a second, the game's Use held, which leaves the seat -----------------------
press left b
wait 0.8
release left b
wait 1.5
read character
expect state != sitting
expect controlledEntity == null
expect log VR controls: on foot within 5

test seats-g-forces
# G-forces in a seat: the ship's pull on the seat moves the eye a few centimetres, presses in the hands, and under a hard
# load greys the view out and makes the astronaut breathe hard. Sitting still on the ground is felt as nothing; lifting
# off and stopping is. The plugin logs each mark the pull or the load crosses ("Seat G: rising ..." and "easing").
# Drill Ship Atmosphere mk.1 from Earth Planet, flown up with A as in seats-cockpit-hand-flight.
plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- Setup: the ship's cockpit, and sit in it ---------------------------------------------------------------------
admin creativeTools
own Drill Ship Atmosphere mk.1
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60
head 0 1.6 0
wait 1
control Cockpit on Drill Ship Atmosphere mk.1
wait 3
read character
expect state == sitting

# ---- Sitting still on the ground: no pull is felt (the planet's gravity is the seat's 1 g, not G) -----------------
wait 3
expect no log Seat G:

# ---- A held lifts the ship for 6 s, letting go the dampeners stop it: the pull crosses the first mark, and eases -------------
press right a
wait 6
release right a
expect log '/Seat G: rising in \S+: the ship pulls [0-9.]+ m.s/' within 6
expect log '/Seat G: easing in \S+: /' within 10

# ---- Pushed into the seat off: the same lift moves the eye by nothing, and the log says so ---------------------------
include vr-option.inc seatGPush false isChecked was_seatGPush
wait 3
press right a
wait 6
release right a
expect log '/Seat G: rising in \S+: .*push 0.0 cm [(]off[)]/' within 6

cleanup
include vr-option.inc seatGPush {was_seatGPush} isChecked _

test seats-passenger-seat
# Getting in and out of a passenger seat with the hands: grip the seat to sit, hold Y to get up.
# A passenger seat has no flight controls, but the buttons and the leave hold work as in any seat.
plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

