test suit-power-hud
# Suit power failing: as the suit's battery runs low, the HUD on the visor flickers and dims, and at zero it and the
# wrist screen go dark; the suit lamp sputters the same way; recharging brings both back with the existing power-on
# effect. A small flashing icon at the HUD's edge marks any of health, food, energy, oxygen or hydrogen at the game's
# own critical mark. Both are settings, on by default (Suit power failing, Low stat warnings at the HUD's edge).
#
# No generic step in this harness reads or sets the suit's battery, hurts it toward empty, or changes a VR plugin's
# own setting (the table in SKILL.md has `hurt AMOUNT` for health and `admin FLAG` for the game's own build/spawn
# flags, nothing for suit energy; a setting is only ever read from the plugin's own file, which `file` steps would
# reach and a public file must not use). So this file cannot drive the suit to low, critical or zero, cannot turn
# either setting off, and cannot watch the HUD or the wrist screen go dark and come back: that needs a real run with
# a battery actually draining, in the headset. What it can check, with the defaults (both settings on) and a fresh
# spawn (a full suit battery): nothing the feature adds shows, flickers or logs while the suit is fully charged - a
# regression check that the feature leaves a healthy suit alone. (Its patches are put on once, as the game starts,
# before any test's log is read, so whether they took hold is not something a test here can see.)

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
wait 2
expect headset steady

# A fresh spawn's suit is full: the HUD is lit as the game draws it, none of the low/critical/out states entered,
# no low-stat icon at the HUD's edge, nothing thrown.
headset hud-full-power.png
expect headset bright
expect no log Suit power: low
